WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:26.780
Unapproved peptides could reach temporary sale while treatment claims are still not fully safety tested. This is Peptides Weekly, episode 4. Education and evidence, never-dosing advice. Political wire quotes the Washington Post on a drafting process, which is policy reporting rather than a patient trial. The paper's account says compounding pharmacies could hand out some of those peptides as marketed treatments and as wellness products.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:26.980
effects.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:31.000
Federal health officials are still writing the regulations around them.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:37.100
On October 1st, this show was tracking compounding rules, and the new piece is that temporary

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.800
sale draft for products the headline still calls unapproved.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:47.600
Stock Twits reported an FDA advisory panel backed four peptides, a panel action rather

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.140
than a published patient study.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:55.440
That item also tied the backing to an overnight rise in hymns' shares and a short bit by

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:01.880
Martin Shkreli. Medical economics, the same day, said the FDA would convene an expert panel

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:08.820
on wider peptide access. Those reports describe meetings, backing, and a share move, not a measured

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:16.560
health outcome. The ASCO post reported a link between GLP1 receptor agonist use and lower colorectal

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:22.420
cancer risk among people with inflammatory bowel disease. The Sacramento Bee and the Raleigh News

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:26.480
an observer, both ran consumer pieces on oral peptide strips.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:32.860
The B says the strips promised needle-free delivery and puts the FDA and researcher view as

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:33.900
the question in play.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:39.160
The news and observer describes dissolving films and asks how the strips work.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:43.240
In the text here, neither piece is a human efficacy measurement.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:49.260
Food Navigator reported that weight regained after GLP1 treatment could be mitigated by

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:49.620
diet.

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:49.760
it.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:55.380
That is a possibility stated in a headline, not a randomized trial result with a number

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:55.900
attached.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:01.920
This week's spotlight is collagen peptides taken by mouth, studied as supplements and

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:07.060
in one paper as a neutrophosimetic ingredient, not as a named approved drug.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:13.760
A 2015 cosmetic dermatology paper says earlier preclinical work suggested these fragments

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:19.600
can support the skin barrier, prompt collagen and hyaluronic acid synthesis, and encourage

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.100
fibroblasts to grow and move. In human skin

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:28.820
plants, an X vivo setup, the peptides induced collagen and glycosaminoglycan

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:33.700
production. That is a tissue finding, not a map of digestion in a living person.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:38.720
The same paper reports two placebo-controlled human trials in which oral

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:43.480
supplementation raised skin hydration after eight weeks by corneometry.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:49.420
Dermal collagen density rows and network fragmentation fell after four weeks on

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:55.040
ultrasound and reflectance confocal microscopy, and both structural changes were still there

00:02:55.040 --> 00:03:02.220
at 12 weeks. A separate randomized placebo-controlled trial enrolled Korean adults aged 19 to 60

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:09.420
with mild to moderate hair damage and no alopecia. After 24 weeks of a low molecular weight collagen

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:16.840
peptide called GT, gloss improved against placebo on a gloss meter and on scanning electron microscopy.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:23.480
Elasticity improved too, judged by tensile strength and hair diameter, and scalp elasticity

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:24.940
rose in the treated group.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:31.220
Participants also rated gloss, elasticity, thickness, texture, fullness, and appearance

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:31.800
as better.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:36.840
No treatment-related adverse events were observed, and the authors called the course

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:39.540
safe and effective for hair condition in that group.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:45.040
The abstract notes earlier preclinical work in which low molecular weight fish collagen

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:50.740
peptides promoted hair regrowth through proliferative signals and less inhibitory signaling,

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:56.080
and it says clinical efficacy for hair damage had not been clearly shown before this trial.

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:01.280
This human study measured damage and shine, not regrowth in alopecia.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:09.260
A pilot randomized double-blind trial followed 22 premenopausal women, 18-35, who ran at least

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:14.580
35 miles a week. For four weeks they took collagen peptides or an isocholoric

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:21.000
maltodextreme placebo, with labs in the early follicular phase. P1NP, a bone

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:27.640
formation marker, showed a group by time interaction at P equals 0.04. It rose

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:34.120
on collagen and did not change on placebo. CTX1, a breakdown marker, had no

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:37.240
significant interaction, P equals 0.13.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:42.720
IL-6 showed a significant interaction at P equals 0.03.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:47.460
The results text both reports a significant S-rankel interaction

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:52.780
at P equals 0.046, and later says no significant interaction

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:56.280
for S-rankel, osteoprategorin, or their ratio,

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:00.180
so that osteoclast signal is not cleanly established.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:06.620
The discussion still says the short course raised a formation marker, shifted osteoclast-related

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:12.660
signaling, and lowered IL-6, and it asks for larger trials with structural bone outcomes.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:20.440
Another randomized double-blind trial followed 53 men with sarcopenia, mean age 72.2 years,

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:22.880
standard deviation 4.68.

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:28.900
All of them did 12 weeks of guided resistance training, three sessions a week, plus either

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:31.300
collagen peptides or a silica placebo.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:38.020
Finisher as a whole gained fat-free mass, bone mass, quadricep strength, and sensory motor

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:42.180
control, and lost fat, each at p less than 0.01.

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:48.960
The collagen arm moved further, fat-free mass up 4.2 kg versus 2.9.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:53.500
Strength up 16.5 Newton meters versus 7.3.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:57.880
Fat mass down 5.4 kg versus 3.5.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:04.160
each comparison P less than 0.05. That extra change belongs to training plus

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:09.540
supplement, not to the peptide by itself. Across this set, fracture prevention is

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:14.920
not shown, alopecia regrowth is not shown, and a blood marker is not a clinical

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:19.920
bone outcome. Only the hair trial states a safety result, and none of these

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:24.800
abstracts test whether a retail bottle matches the study material. One thing

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:30.200
Being worth knowing is that a cancer risk link for GLP1 drugs in inflammatory bowel disease

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:33.700
does not mean those drugs have been shown to prevent cancer.

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:40.240
Another is that the collagen human trials measure skin structure, hair condition, bone markers,

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:44.920
and training-related body composition, which is not the same as treating a disease.

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:51.540
A third is that temporary sale drafts and advisory panel backing are about access and process,

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:57.340
not prove those peptides work in people. That's peptides weekly. This show is

00:06:57.340 --> 00:07:01.980
education, not medical advice. Talk to your own clinician before acting on

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:07.200
anything you heard. I'm Patrick in Vancouver. See you next week. And before you

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:12.340
go, this show is part of the Nerra network, a family of daily podcasts on tech,

